Retrogram
=========

Retrogram is a combined work distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 (see LICENSE).

It is derived from:

  * Nagram XF (https://github.com/Keeperorowner/NagramXF), GPL-3.0, itself a
    fork of Nagram X and including features derived from exteraGram and AyuGram.
  * Telegram for Android (https://github.com/DrKLO/Telegram), whose source
    headers grant "GNU GPL version 2 or later"; that grant permits distribution
    of the combined work under GPL-3.0.

All upstream copyright and license headers are kept in the files they appear in.
Do not remove them when editing or reviving code.

Provenance notes
----------------

  * See docs/compliance.md for the provenance map (which namespace comes from which upstream project), the restriction-bypass defaults, analytics and credentials.
  * Nagram XF states that it contains code reverse-engineered from closed-source
    forks. Retrogram tracks the affected modules as a legal risk (PLAN.md §4) and
    prefers clean-room replacements.
  * Code revived from older Telegram releases carries a header comment with the
    source commit and path.
  * Graph Messenger is used only as a behavioural reference. No code from it is
    copied or decompiled.

